## Route

A route is `routes/<route>/ROUTE.md` under the directory this file is in, which the host names when it loads this skill.

The arguments are the text this skill was invoked with. Their first word is the route: read that route's `ROUTE.md` and follow it, with the rest as its arguments. If the first word is not a route, the arguments are the task; with no arguments, the task is the one at hand. Take the route whose row fits the task, and when none plainly does, the default, `{{DEFAULT_ROUTE}}`.

A route is a document to read, never a skill to call: no skill is named after one.

| Route | In short | Starts it |
| --- | --- | --- |
{{ROUTE_ROWS}}

After a compaction, read your route's `ROUTE.md` again before going on: the host re-attaches this skill, not a file read by path.
